	affiliations = {Pacific Northwest National Laboratory, Richland, United States; Pacific Northwest National Laboratory, Richland, United States},
	abstract = {Effective data discovery is crucial for driving progress in complex fields like wind energy research, where large volumes of scientific studies, environmental data, and regulatory documents need to be explored and synthesized. Traditional search methods, primarily based on keyword matching, often fail to provide precise results due to the fragmented nature of the data, which is distributed across various databases and presented in different formats such as text, images, maps, etc. This paper proposes an AI-driven framework designed to streamline the discovery and integration of wind energy-related data utilizing advanced multimodal techniques. This framework integrates data from the Tethys database, curating environmental and regulatory documents, and transforming them into a unified multimodal vector database. This system leverages Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to perform sophisticated multimodal search and generative chat applications. The proposed framework improves decision making in wind energy projects by enabling efficient access to both textual and visual information. Our results demonstrate how the AI capabilities of the system reduce time and effort in data discovery, offering a comprehensive tool for research, planning, and execution in the development of wind energy. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
