	abstract = {Company reviews play an essential role as digital forces in modern society because they serve as the foundation for how people understand the market and form industrial plans. An AI system that processes company review sentiments through Natural Language Processing (NLP) stands at the core of this research framework. Customer feedback data sets can support the analysis through text preprocessing and TF-IDF feature extraction, while Naive Bayes, logistic regression, and random forest models provide classification functionalities. The assessment criteria used in this study indicate that the easy-to-understand logistic regression emerges as the preferred model for analysis of accuracy, precision-recall, and F1-score measurements. Customers can identify crucial emotional patterns throughout their feedback through the combination of word clouds with sentiment distribution graphs. Organizations metamorphose into data insights powerhouses where NLP functions with ML because both technologies extract clear business information from enormous text datasets instantly. The final project demonstrates expert-level sentiment analytics through AI as well as fundamental structures required for building comprehensive customer experience management systems at scale and developed a system function in multiple fields, including product assessment, worker feedback assessment, and social media content evaluation. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
