	affiliations = {Al-Zaytoonah University of Jordan, Department of Software Engineering, Amman, Jordan; Al-Ahliyya Amman University, Medical Engineering Department, Amman, Jordan; Middle East University Jordan, Software Engineering Department, Amman, Jordan; Zarqa University, Department of Computer Science, Zarqa, Jordan; Al-Balqa Applied University, Department of Electrical Engineering, Salt, Jordan},
	abstract = {Software project management (PM) is increasingly challenged by the need to accurately predict delivery timelines and efficiently allocate resources in dynamic and complex development environments. Traditional estimation and planning methods often fall short due to their reliance on static assumptions, expert judgment, and limited adaptability to changing project conditions. This paper investigates the application of artificial intelligence (AI) models such as machine learning (ML), natural language processing (NLP), and optimization algorithms to enhance software project planning and execution. Thus, the study presents a framework for predicting delivery times using supervised learning models and optimizing resource allocation through intelligent scheduling and reinforcement learning. The methodology is evaluated through real-world case studies from industry, demonstrating notable improvements in workload balancing, estimation accuracy, and project efficiency. The results highlight the potential of AI to transform software project management by enabling data-driven, adaptive, and proactive decision-making. The paper concludes with a discussion of current challenges, such as data quality and model interpretability, and outlines future research directions. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
