	abstract = {In recent years, a great deal of studies has been done on how to develop the basis of an artificial intelligence business model. One matter, though, remained unresolved and was difficult to comprehend. How organizations alter and refine their AI business model architecture to achieve ongoing value generation has been essential for aspirant and progressive managers and researchers alike. Organizations that successfully create value over long periods of time plan, adapt, and restart their business models using AI technologies to support this value creation. A summary of findings from a study project on continuously growing organizations is provided. This paper classifies three risky competencies, namely, a focus on identifying and utilizing creative business opportunities, a well-adjusted use of resources, and achieving clarity between management, ethos, and employee responsibilities. Taken together, these competencies determine key maneuvering schedules. In our conclusion, we highlight the implications for AI business model research and specialists and offer executives a tool that enables them to replicate and categorize risky issues related to evolving and changing their business model to sustain value generation. In this essay, we attempt to examine the essential components of the commercial Model Framework, which will completely alter the environment of the commercial market. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
