	affiliations = {},
	abstract = {This study explores the integration of generative artificial intelligence (Gen AI) technology into the operations of Bravo, a boutique branding consultancy firm. With operational challenges such as limited resources, rapid technological advancements, and changing consumer preferences, Bravo seeks to leverage Gen AI to enhance productivity, streamline workflows, and optimise resource management. The research investigates how Gen AI can be integrated into Bravo's operational framework and assesses its impact on team productivity and operational efficiency. The study is divided into several key experiments designed to test the practical applications and benefits of Gen AI in Bravo's specific context. These experiments include the development of an AI-powered knowledge base (KB), assisting in bespoke project planning, and creating a self-updating knowledge management system (KMS). The findings demonstrate that Gen AI can significantly streamline information creation, reduce managerial workload, and improve project management efficiency. Gen AI's capability to enrich and evolve the company's KB continuously through real-time data analysis is highlighted. The research concludes with recommendations for Bravo and similar boutique firms. These include adopting a living, breathing KB, leveraging Gen AI for tedious and complex tasks, implementing Gen AI across small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), investing in Gen AI training and development, and pursuing continuous innovation with Gen AI. Bravo's successful implementation of Gen AI is a model for other organisations, emphasising its potential to transform operations, enhance productivity, and ensure adaptability to changing market dynamics. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
