	affiliations = {Lekha Wireless Solutions Pvt. Ltd., Bengaluru, India},
	abstract = {Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS) encompass a broad range of technologies and strategies that aim to provide innovative services relating to different modes of transport and traffic management and enable users to be better informed and make safer, more coordinated, and smarter use of transport networks. One of the main pillars of 6G technology, Integrated Sensing and Communication (ISAC), integrates communication and sensing capabilities into a single system. ISAC can significantly enhance ITS by improving the way vehicles and infrastructure interact, leading to more efficient, safe, and sustainable transportation networks. Moreover, Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) can provide aerial data to complement ground-based sensors in ITS, leading to more comprehensive traffic analyses. The synergy between UAVs, ITS and ISAC has the potential to create smarter, safer, and more efficient transportation networks. In ISAC systems, various sensing modes can be utilized to enhance the performance of both sensing and communication functions. Each mode has its specific applications, advantages, and limitations. In this work, we propose a learning based sensing mode selection for ISAC in ITS. By applying learning-based approaches to sensing mode selection in ISAC, ITS can enhance the operational effectiveness across diverse environments. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
