	abstract = {The sustainable management of natural resources and the promotion of responsible consumption and production patterns are critical components of the United Nations' Sustainable Development Goal 12. The electrical sector, as a significant consumer of resources and a vital infrastructure provider, holds substantial potential to contribute to these objectives. This paper presents the experiences of four Brazilian research groups - GRVA, CEASB, Voxar Labs and LabCG - in leveraging Artificial Intelligence and Extended Reality technologies to foster sustainability within the electrical sector. Each group has developed projects that integrate AI and/or XR to optimize resource utilization, automate fault detection, reduce waste generation, and promote sustainable practices. Through detailed analyses of these initiatives, we highlight the methodologies employed, technologies utilized, and outcomes achieved. The findings demonstrate the tangible benefits and real-world impact of applying AI-based XR solutions, including enhanced operational efficiency, improved maintenance processes, and increased stakeholder engagement. By showcasing these case studies, we illustrate how AI and XR technologies can effectively address key challenges in the electrical sector, align with specific SDG 12 targets, and inspire further research and collaboration toward sustainable development. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
