	abstract = {This paper introduces a smart mobile application aimed at revolutionizing the way users donate, exchange, and organize outfits, leveraging Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Machine Learning (ML) to address the growing concerns of sustainability in the fashion industry. The problem of textile waste and unsustainable consumption patterns necessitates innovative solutions for clothing redistribution. Our application proposes a novel approach by integrating a user-friendly interface developed with FlutterFlow, an intelligent backend powered by Python and the Open AI API, and Firebase for database management. We tackled challenges such as personalizing user experiences through AI-driven recommendations and ensuring scalability under varying user loads. Through meticulous experiments, including testing the AI's recommendation accuracy and the system's load capacity, we demonstrated the application's effectiveness in promoting sustainable fashion practices. Our results highlight significant improvements in user engagement and system performance, suggesting that our application offers a practical, scalable solution for sustainable wardrobe management. Ultimately, this project not only contributes to reducing fashion waste but also empowers users to make environmentally conscious decisions in their clothing consumption. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
