	abstract = {Traditional human resource management processes are being revolutionised as a result of the incorporation of artificial intelligence (AI) into human resource analytics. The purpose of this study is to investigate the transformative element of AI-enabled HR analytics in the context of rethinking the fundamental roles of human resource management. By utilising technology that is powered by artificial intelligence, organisations can improve data-driven decision-making, improve gift accession, and optimise hand performance and engagement. The purpose of this project is to investigate how artificial intelligence-driven perceptivity can facilitate extra individualised hand gestures, simplify reclamation procedures, and provide support for predictive analytics for pool planning. In addition, the study investigates the difficulties and ethical concerns that are linked with the implementation of AI in human resources, with a particular focus on the importance of transparency and justice. Specifically, the findings highlight the potential for artificial intelligence to not only improve efficiency but also to encourage a more strategic and forward-thinking approach to human resource management. Providing interpreters and scholars working on the subject with new perspectives, this investigation contributes to the ongoing conversation about how artificial intelligence is influencing the future of human resources. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
