	abstract = {With the objective of the governments to attain economic growth, effectiveness, and efficiency in public service delivery, it behooves upon the government to harness the state-of-the-art information and communication technology (ICT). Of late, artificial intelligence (AI) has been dominating the ICT space on account of its multifarious applications in different sectors, like education, health, science, management, and the like. Governments across the world are spearheading initiatives to make public service delivery hassle-free and congenial for the users. Against this backdrop, smart cities are furthering the application of state-of-the-art technologies in public service delivery as well. However, as far as the Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC) constituents, i.e., Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Oman, Kuwait, Bahrain, and the United Arab Emirates, are concerned, the smart city initiatives are still in their nascent stages; notwithstanding the range of possibilities unleashed by the application of AI. This chapter underlines the opportunities and challenges of the application of AI in the public service delivery, including services designed for the private sector. Given the cultural and infrastructural divide across the GCC region, there are multifold challenges the governments face to integrate AI in public service delivery formats in the smart city projects. However, with sustained political will, manpower training and optimum budgeting, the benefits of AI in public service delivery may be better realized. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
