	affiliations = {Universiti Teknologi PETRONAS, Seri Iskandar, Malaysia; Liverpool John Moores University, Liverpool, United Kingdom; CECOS University of IT & Emerging Sciences, Department of Civil Engineering, Peshawar, Pakistan; Griffith University, Brisbane, Australia},
	abstract = {The chapter provides a comprehensive exploration of the transformative potential of Industry 4.0 and artificial intelligence (AI) within the construction sector. Industry 4.0, often referred to as the Fourth Industrial Revolution, represents a paradigm shift driven by cutting-edge digital technologies, including AI, machine learning, and internet of things (IoT), which are reshaping traditional construction processes. The construction industry, a substantial contributor to global GDP, has historically faced challenges related to productivity, technological adoption, and sustainability. However, with the advent of Industry 4.0, the sector stands on the brink of a technological revolution. AI, in conjunction with material science, is unlocking unprecedented opportunities for increased efficiency, sustainability, and cost-effectiveness in construction projects. This chapter dives deep into the core principles of Industry 4.0, its historical evolution, and the key technologies driving this revolution, such as AI, robotics, IoT, and big data analytics. It explains how these technologies are impacting construction, transforming processes, enabling automation, and revolutionizing project management through concepts like digital twins and virtual reality. Furthermore, the challenges and opportunities AI presents to the construction industry, including data quality, workforce adaptation, legal considerations, and the economic impacts of AI adoption are discussed. Throughout the chapter, an emphasis is placed on the importance of collaboration, change management, and fostering a culture of digital innovation within construction organizations. The integration of Industry 4.0, supported by a robust framework of standardization and best practices, ensures the sector's readiness to embrace the future. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
