	affiliations = {Shandong Vocational College of Science and Technology, Weifang, China},
	abstract = {In the enterprise financial management (EFM) industry, artificial intelligence (AI) has brought great impact to the traditional EFM mode, and also promoted the transformation of EFM mode and financial personnel. In this article, the data-driven idea and AI algorithm are used to establish a pre-alarm model of EFM, so as to improve the decision-making efficiency and reliability of EFM system. The feasibility of EFM system is analyzed through the simulation experiment of financial data. The simulation results show that the enterprise financial decision-making model in this article is more accurate in predicting the financial situation of enterprises. Compared with the traditional support vector machine (SVM) algorithm, the recall is increased by 17.25% and the accuracy rate is increased by 18.88%. Applying the EFM method proposed in this article to enterprises and even other fields can optimize the financial capital flow, thus promoting the maximization of economic benefits under the premise of ensuring social benefits. Enterprise managers can track the financial status of enterprises and the use of project funds at any time and anywhere, change the way of publishing in the past, and combine financial and non-financial information with the continuous growth of big data to make information docking more convenient and fast. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
