	abstract = {At present, spacecraft has the characteristics of complex product composition, technical difficulty, manufacturing process and project management. To meet the needs of improving the quality, efficiency and benefit of spacecraft complex structure products, the construction and improvement of a new generation of scientific research and production information system will be carried out. In this paper, an AI (artificial intelligence) algorithm-based digital integrated platform for automated manufacturing of spacecraft complex structures is established, and various computing and storage resources are optimized, reorganized and scheduled by virtual machines to improve resource utilization. By simulating the assembly sequence, it can be verified whether the operating space is spacious enough, whether the tools used meet the requirements, whether the fixture structure is reliable, and whether there is interference with the product. A quality diagnosis model for the automated manufacturing process of spacecraft complex structures based on the combination of rough set theory and BPNN (BP neural network) in information processing has been established. The diagnosis results of an example show that the BPNN method can greatly improve the diagnosis efficiency and reduce the diagnosis cost, which can provide an effective reference for solving the quality diagnosis in modern spacecraft engineering. It can gradually realize the digital design, simulation, manufacturing, maintenance/repair of spacecraft, and completely digitize the whole life cycle from product design, process design, parts manufacturing, assembly and assembly, maintenance and repair. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
