	doi = {10.1007/978-3-662-66509-1_14},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85160506456&doi=10.1007%2F978-3-662-66509-1_14&partnerID=40&md5=f93aa9915d5ad5f3e1d0b11ee9ac4d62},
	affiliations = {dataMatters GmbH, Koln, Germany},
	abstract = {With the increasing complexity of analytical questions in companies, the development of data-driven services using techniques of artificial intelligence (AI) or machine learning (ML) are increasingly in the focus, in addition to simple methods such as visualizations and simple statistical evaluations. However, often such projects fail due to the available data basis, which, due to a lack of diversity and size, entails the risk of only partially meaningful results. Therefore, what is needed is a way to make data sources networkable so that relevant data can be easily purchased for the development of a service. senseering GmbH has taken on this task and created the MyDataEconomy, a decentralized data management network, that handles the simple exchange of data between two or more parties in the network securely and quickly.. In order to also exploit the value of one’s own data and not only make it available to others in the network, it must also be possible for every network participant to visualize and analyze his own data. For this purpose, the MyDataEconomy was extended with analysis and visualization modules on the network nodes and equipped with connectors for the connection of machines, sensors or other data sources. The result is a globally usable data economy in which every participant can experience the added value of internal and external data in interaction. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
